    <tags>relay server messenger p2p rendezvous</tags>
    <summary>Nexa Beep relay server (rendezvous, hole punching, relay fallback)</summary>
    <description>
The relay server for the Nexa Beep messenger. It only does presence (rotating
RIDs), rendezvous / hole-punching observation, and blind relaying — conversation
content is end-to-end encrypted, so the server cannot read it, and nothing is
stored (it is a pipe, not a buffer).

- Single executable, no runtime dependencies
- Firewall: open TCP and UDP on the same port (47300 by default)
- The first run creates the server identity key (beepd.key) and prints the
  fingerprint that clients pin
- Operations guide: docs/41-beepd-ops-guide.md
- How it works: docs/42-relay-rendezvous-walkthrough.md

License: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 (noncommercial use).
    </description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
